WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: ar

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
The game first appeared for the poor people

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.000
before rich people

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.240
Where deals are made in hundreds of millions of dollars

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:11.398
Brands of its clubs are worth

00:00:11.399 --> 00:00:12.920
Billions $$

00:00:12.921 --> 00:00:16.071
and its legends are welcomed like kings

00:00:16.072 --> 00:00:19.823
Its players get astronomical sums 

00:00:19.824 --> 00:00:22.360
Where politicians and riches involve investments

00:00:22.361 --> 00:00:25.000
and the economies of countries rely on it

00:00:25.001 --> 00:00:29.210
Its club’s budgets compete large companies 

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.148
With millions of workers around the world

00:00:32.148 --> 00:00:35.148
Sponsored by large banks and famous brands 

00:00:35.148 --> 00:00:39.462
It’s a safe place for capitalists

00:00:39.478 --> 00:00:43.541
How does football make its huge profits?

00:00:43.541 --> 00:00:46.520
TV broadcasting rights

00:00:46.521 --> 00:00:48.750
A giant financial cycle 

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.320
that starts with paying the annual subscription 

00:00:51.321 --> 00:00:53.738
and ends in the pockets of players &amp; clubs

00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:57.886
The amount paid depends on the power and popularity of the league

00:00:57.886 --> 00:01:00.000
Television networks 

00:01:00.001 --> 00:01:01.793
and Live streaming sites

00:01:01.793 --> 00:01:03.022
such as Amazon

00:01:03.022 --> 00:01:05.856
sign fictional contracts to buy the rights

00:01:05.856 --> 00:01:10.000
to broadcast league matches from local federations

00:01:10.001 --> 00:01:12.001
The money is distributed to the clubs 

00:01:12.001 --> 00:01:14.001
according to its rank

00:01:14.002 --> 00:01:16.760
popularity and attraction to the viewer

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:21.115
without forgetting to deduct a portion of it for the local federations.

00:01:21.115 --> 00:01:26.054
The English Premier League is the most expensive contract amongst world leagues

00:01:26.054 --> 00:01:36.183
If the rights to broadcast are sold in 2019-2022 for 4.5 billion pounds

00:01:36.184 --> 00:01:44.270
The share of Liverpool, the penultimate season titleholder, was 139 million pounds

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:49.720
while Norwich City, last rank, received 92 million

00:01:49.721 --> 00:01:52.720
Match Tickets

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.120
Continuous and semi-guaranteed income

00:01:55.121 --> 00:01:57.997
that depends on the loyalty of fans to their team

00:01:57.997 --> 00:02:00.289
and their attendance at the stadiums

00:02:00.289 --> 00:02:02.873
Ticket price varies amongst teams 

00:02:02.873 --> 00:02:04.600
and tournaments

00:02:08.041 --> 00:02:10.960
In the Europe Champions League

00:02:10.961 --> 00:02:12.732
prices become higher

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.232
according to the tournament roles

00:02:15.859 --> 00:02:20.000
The price of a first-class ticket for the 2019 final 

00:02:20.466 --> 00:02:23.112
reached $ 667

00:02:23.135 --> 00:02:27.178
and was sold on the black market

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.720
for thousands of dollars $$

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:31.512
The ticket price is sometimes used as

00:02:31.513 --> 00:02:34.160
a pressure means on guest team fans

00:02:34.161 --> 00:02:35.369
by raising the price 

00:02:35.369 --> 00:02:37.994
of tickets for obstructing their attendance at the stadium.

00:02:40.441 --> 00:02:41.232
Barcelona FC

00:02:41.232 --> 00:02:43.128
sold tickets for its matches 

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:45.629
against Liverpool and Manchester United 

00:02:45.629 --> 00:02:49.067
in the 2019 Champions League 

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.160
at the Camp Nou 

00:02:51.202 --> 00:02:53.202
for 119 Euros € 

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.786
Manchester United responded similarly to the Catalan fans 

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:58.600
in the second leg

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.183
before UEFA intervened

00:03:00.183 --> 00:03:03.038
and it set the ceiling for the visiting fans’ ticket 

00:03:03.038 --> 00:03:04.080
at 70 Euros

00:03:04.894 --> 00:03:07.603
But it's a little different for the local leagues

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.043
Ticket prices are set before the season begins

00:03:11.587 --> 00:03:15.921
as annual subscriptions to members of the public

00:03:15.944 --> 00:03:17.756
Arsenal, for example

00:03:17.757 --> 00:03:20.000
sells tickets  

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.646
taking into consideration the quality of the seat class

00:03:23.607 --> 00:03:25.607
at an average price of £97

00:03:30.161 --> 00:03:32.161
while the average price of a ticket for Hull City 

00:03:33.935 --> 00:03:34.872
is £36

00:03:35.621 --> 00:03:37.621
All these guaranteed tickets profits 

00:03:37.621 --> 00:03:40.288
allowed clubs to spend hundreds of millions

00:03:40.289 --> 00:03:42.810
to build new bigger stadiums

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.280
or expand their stadiums

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:49.823
Shirt Sales

00:03:49.824 --> 00:03:52.658
It’s an important factor that clubs 

00:03:52.659 --> 00:03:56.040
rely on to supplement their treasuries with tens of millions annually

00:03:56.041 --> 00:03:57.249
It targets the fan's admiration 

00:03:57.249 --> 00:04:00.520
for the shirt design for the new season

00:04:00.681 --> 00:04:03.348
The percentage of sales increases according to the popularity of the team 

00:04:03.348 --> 00:04:05.827
and the weight of the names of players in its ranks

00:04:05.827 --> 00:04:10.683
and it may become standard when the club attracts a famous or legendary player

00:04:10.684 --> 00:04:13.288
But what followers do not know is that 

00:04:13.384 --> 00:04:17.593
clubs receive a small share of the profits from shirt sales!

00:04:17.761 --> 00:04:20.907
Sponsors, like Adidas, Nike, and others

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:25.243
purchase team T-shirt rights in long-term contracts

00:04:25.266 --> 00:04:27.266
Then T-shirts are manufactured 

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:30.558
and sold in own and club’s stores in the world

00:04:30.559 --> 00:04:34.539
which gives it the largest profit percentage

00:04:34.539 --> 00:04:37.456
For example, Nike concluded a deal

00:04:37.457 --> 00:04:40.520
with Liverpool FC over a period of 5 years

00:04:40.521 --> 00:04:42.521
with a value of $200 million

00:04:42.522 --> 00:04:47.628
which the club would receive a 20% commission from the sales percentage.

00:04:47.755 --> 00:04:50.000
And if you see it as a small percentage

00:04:50.001 --> 00:04:54.711
the surprise is that it is one of the highest commissions that a team can receive!

00:04:54.711 --> 00:05:00.254
Commissions usually range from 7.5% to 15% max!

00:05:01.923 --> 00:05:05.799
Financial Rewards

00:05:06.081 --> 00:05:08.769
The more the team wins and plays better

00:05:08.833 --> 00:05:13.647
the more profits it gets

00:05:14.437 --> 00:05:17.020
Participation in the EU Champions League

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:20.166
generates fantastic profits for clubs

00:05:20.281 --> 00:05:22.406
This participation guarantees 

00:05:22.407 --> 00:05:24.740
15 million euros for the club 

00:05:24.763 --> 00:05:29.243
Winning each match means 2.7 million Euros

00:05:29.349 --> 00:05:31.787
&amp; Draw means 900,000 Euros

00:05:31.851 --> 00:05:35.769
The winner of the tournament earns 19 million Euros

00:05:35.989 --> 00:05:39.573
which means that he may win a total prize money 

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:42.971
about 80 million Euros

00:05:43.081 --> 00:05:47.832
Clubs also receive good money prizes upon winning local leagues

00:05:50.398 --> 00:05:53.044
Sponsorship Rights

00:05:53.241 --> 00:05:58.013
Football clubs use their Shirts as a moving billboard!

00:05:58.121 --> 00:06:02.997
And among its stadiums, as an arena for promoting the contracted brands

00:06:02.998 --> 00:06:07.812
Real Madrid has a fictional contract with Emirates Airlines

00:06:07.835 --> 00:06:09.543
for 5-years

00:06:09.629 --> 00:06:12.965
where it earns $82.5 million 

00:06:12.965 --> 00:06:14.965
every season!

00:06:15.175 --> 00:06:18.988
Followed by Tottenham contract with the insurance company AIA

00:06:19.052 --> 00:06:21.719
with a $50 million /Season 

00:06:22.121 --> 00:06:25.392
Then Manchester United, who signed a new five-year contract 

00:06:25.425 --> 00:06:30.238
early this season with TeamViewer

00:06:30.448 --> 00:06:32.719
and provides the club's treasury with

00:06:32.784 --> 00:06:37.369
£ 47 million each season

00:06:37.433 --> 00:06:39.433
Some clubs use T-shirt 

00:06:39.434 --> 00:06:44.498
to advertise slogans &amp; brands on the sleeves or backside

00:06:44.696 --> 00:06:47.884
Clubs sometimes take advantage of everything related to them

00:06:47.989 --> 00:06:50.281
to the point of changing the name of their stadium!

00:06:50.304 --> 00:06:52.304
A club like Arsenal

00:06:52.305 --> 00:06:56.118
 not only signed a sponsorship contract with Emirates Airlines

00:06:56.183 --> 00:07:01.684
but also named its stadium "Emirates Stadium", in 2006

00:07:01.874 --> 00:07:03.874
after buying Name Rights

00:07:03.874 --> 00:07:08.375
until 2028!

00:07:09.241 --> 00:07:13.867
as well as organizing a friendly tournament - Emirates Cup

00:07:15.314 --> 00:07:17.314
Selling Players

00:07:18.097 --> 00:07:20.660
A source that brings money for the clubs 

00:07:20.703 --> 00:07:23.495
and puts others in an economic deficit

00:07:23.601 --> 00:07:27.935
Some clubs spend hundreds of millions annually to buy new players

00:07:28.083 --> 00:07:30.083
Some of them write the history 

00:07:30.083 --> 00:07:35.814
and others are a disaster for the club and an economic burden

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:40.925
Benfica FC was the most profitable club 

00:07:40.925 --> 00:07:42.925
through selling players

00:07:42.926 --> 00:07:44.926
In the last ten years, 

00:07:46.084 --> 00:07:48.480
players sold at £ 1 Billion

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:50.480
One of them is Joao Felix

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:52.480
who moved to Atletico Madrid 

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:55.772
for £ 101 Million

00:07:55.772 --> 00:07:59.398
The selling club benefits from the deal full amount 

00:07:59.483 --> 00:08:01.983
without giving anything to the sold player

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:05.672
unless the contract includes a sum of money called 

00:08:05.672 --> 00:08:07.672
The "Contract Bonus"

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:11.902
However, a club like Barcelona has spent more than

00:08:12.048 --> 00:08:16.592
1 Billion Euros to buy new players in the last five years

00:08:16.823 --> 00:08:21.199
3 of them cost the club's more than 400 Million Euros

00:08:21.321 --> 00:08:23.321
in addition to their large salaries

00:08:23.698 --> 00:08:25.698
as a result, the club entered into a financial crisis 

00:08:25.699 --> 00:08:28.595
with no solution until now

00:08:28.701 --> 00:08:32.680
After an era when La Masia academy was a Human factory

00:08:32.681 --> 00:08:34.681
supplying the club with the finest players

00:08:34.871 --> 00:08:38.163
and earn large sums of money upon their sale

00:08:38.186 --> 00:08:41.999
Sometimes, clubs get players for free!

00:08:41.999 --> 00:08:43.999
without paying anything to the seller club 

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.709
because of the expired contract

00:08:47.921 --> 00:08:49.921
The Argentine Lionel Messi's deal 

00:08:50.277 --> 00:08:53.903
to Paris Saint-Germain is the best example of this

00:08:54.113 --> 00:08:55.134
I mean it's unbelievable 

00:08:55.135 --> 00:08:56.843
that we have the best player in the world 

00:08:57.469 --> 00:08:59.469
at Paris Saint-Germain

00:08:59.469 --> 00:09:00.215
for the past three days! 

00:09:00.215 --> 00:09:04.200
Calls we received from sponsors were unbelievable,

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:07.513
I did not expect this number!

00:09:07.598 --> 00:09:11.453
The sources of profit are many, diverse, and uncountable

00:09:11.697 --> 00:09:13.520
fills the pockets of the players 

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:17.417
and load tons of money into their bank accounts!

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:21.019
The game was a haven for the poor people to escape from life suffering

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:24.290
stolen in front of their eyes

00:09:24.792 --> 00:09:28.160
They neither afford to buy their favorite team's T-shirt

00:09:28.286 --> 00:09:31.224
nor enter the stadium to cheer their favorite team

00:09:31.321 --> 00:09:35.176
&amp; some don't even have the luxury of paying a TV subscription

00:09:35.199 --> 00:09:38.929
How long will the crazy football spending last?

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:43.820
Does ever a day come when we witness an economic setback into it

00:09:44.176 --> 00:09:46.176
and bring it back to its old days?!

00:09:51.824 --> 00:09:57.576
Football.. the  Stolen poor sport

